# runs/ is deliberately not ignored here: round records and gate reports are
# committed on purpose, so ignoring the tree would hide new captures from
# git status and force `git add -f` for the records that stay. Captures are
# kept out of the code index by .codeindexignore, not by git.
!uv.lock
